      "side": 1,
      "message": "The idea was to not let kernel headers should never use the dynamic page shift.\n\nIf a header function needs to know the process page size, it takes mm or vma explicitly (like mm_pte_shift(mm) or vma_pages(vma)).\n\np3s_user_pages.h is strictly for C source files (translation units) that opt in at the very end of their include list so only that specific file evaluates PAGE_SIZE dynamically.\n\nUpdated the commit description to clarify that header files must never use dynamic page size and must never include p3s_user_pages.h; and added a compile-time check in include/linux/p3s_user_pages.h",
